title: Loom vs gstack — Supplementary Dimensions (beyond the 7-axis M-09 scorecard)
methodology: Same evidence-anchored comparative rigor as scorecard-rerun.toon; four dimensions the original 7-axis rubric did not isolate (they were partly folded into ops-polish/prompt-assets). Assessed 2026-07-04. gstack read at /tmp/gstack-review. Scores 0-10, honest, not massaged.
relatedTo: planning/reports/scorecard-rerun.toon
note: These are supplementary/advisory — NOT part of the frozen F-25 acceptance rubric. They inform where Loom genuinely leads/trails beyond the seven pinned dimensions.
dimensions[4]{dimension,loom,gstack,delta,verdict}:
  installability,7,8,-1,"gstack leads — 10 host configs vs Loom's 4, auto host-detection, dependency auto-install, Windows copy-fallback, per-host SKILL templating, team/vendored modes. Loom wins ONLY the integrity axis: a real fail-closed checksum gate + EXIT rollback trap that gstack's git-clone setup does not attempt."
  upgradeability,9,6,3,"Loom leads decisively — 24-schema version registry + chained migrations (v2->v3->v4) + dry-run + backup + SHA256-chain-verified rollback + structural PLAN/ROADMAP upgraders. gstack = git fetch+reset --hard then re-run setup, one-way bash migration patches, coarse .bak rollback. gstack edges only on update-delivery UX (remote poll/auto-upgrade) + a clean single VERSION file."
  status-state-awareness,8,5,3,"Loom leads decisively — rich contract-backed live statusline (Active/Idle segments: command/phase/wave/agents/pass-fail/rate) + per-agent heartbeat monitoring + loom-status/loom-next + pause/resume. gstack has NO statusline anywhere (grep-confirmed); its dashboards surface community/Supabase telemetry, not the user's own run. Parity only on multi-workspace (landing-report both sides) + resumability."
  knowledge-memory-layer,7,8,-1,"gstack (gbrain) leads on RAW RETRIEVAL — semantic/vector search (voyage-code-3/OpenAI embeddings over PGLite/Postgres) + symbol call-graph (code-def/refs/callers/callees) + cross-machine/team-shared memory via git-synced MCP brain. Loom's wiki is keyword+2-hop-graph over ~40 curated TOON pages, repo-local, no embeddings. BUT Loom trades scale-recall for: curation+legibility, in-repo version control, PUSH auto-injection (SessionStart hook vs gbrain's pull-when-remembered), an ENFORCEMENT-wired judgment layer (regressions w/ detectionRegex in reviewer gates — gbrain has no analog), and no Postgres/embeddings-API/25min-sync operational cost. Gap is architectural + scale, real but not a chasm; only bites hard at thousands-of-pages / multi-machine history."
summary:
  loomLeads[2]: upgradeability (9v6), status-state-awareness (8v5)
  gstackLeads[2]: installability (8v7), knowledge-memory-layer (8v7)
  netLoom: 31
  netGstack: 27
  pattern: "Loom's edge is engineered internal machinery (crypto-verified rollback, schema registry, contract-backed live statusline w/ per-agent heartbeats). gstack's edge is boundary breadth+polish (10-host install, dep auto-install, Windows fallback) and a mature embedding-backed shared brain. Loom trails on multi-host REACH and first-run convenience + large-scale semantic recall; it does NOT trail on safety or run-visibility."
gapsWorthNoting[2]{gap,severity,recommendation}:
  installability-multihost,moderate,"Loom supports 4 hosts vs gstack 10; no auto host-detect / dep auto-install / Windows fallback. Closable if multi-host reach becomes a goal — mechanical, not architectural."
  gbrain-semantic-recall,"major-but-optional (user-acknowledged)","Architectural: embeddings + symbol call-graph + cross-machine brain. Loom's curated+push+enforced model is a coherent lower-cost alternative; only worth closing if Loom targets very large codebases / long multi-machine histories."
